WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:02.377
When I first received the script

00:00:02.377 --> 00:00:03.920
it came off the page visually at me

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.965
there were so many things that I just wanted to get my hands on to design.

00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:13.638
The characters are fully rounded. It's got great story arcs.

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:17.142
It just felt like there was quite a lot of storytelling that could be done with costume there.

00:00:18.226 --> 00:00:23.648
The clothes have been just such a joy to wear.

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:30.739
Cora's costume really goes from somebody who is very corseted and restricted.

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:33.700
I think the way Jane has dressed her

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.370
it feels very contemporary in a way that also is very accurate.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:44.502
When we meet Cora her aesthetic has been totally dictated by a very controlling man.

00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:49.466
There's a Japanese thread in Michael's house, which is where we first meet Cora.

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:53.011
There's a sculpted, Origami feel to some of the costumes.

00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:58.266
This fabric we found quite early in the shoot, this has the Kintsugi vase effect.

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:01.519
And the broken vase, once repaired, and repaired with gold

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:03.396
they're seen as more beautiful than the original.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.565
And this is how Michael saw Cora.

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:10.236
Told me he wanted to break me, and mend me with gold.

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:14.157
These are the earrings that Cora wears to Michael's funeral

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:16.743
and she decides to rid herself of them

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.538
and then she gets to Essex and she's in emotional recovery.

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:21.956
That all starts to show in her clothes.

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:27.087
She's been in such a controlled environment for so long.

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:30.840
Then in Essex she gets to define for herself who she is.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.010
Her hair loosens and relaxes

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.720
and so does her wardrobe

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.555
and, of course, so does her spirit.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:45.105
Cora arrives in Aldwinter in Essex

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.274
where she meets the local reverend, Will Ransome.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:52.070
He'll wear the uniform, because he knows it's necessary,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.864
but he'd rather be out on the marshes being blown about.

00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:59.119
This is Will's scarf that he lends to Cora.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.496
The scarf plays an emotional role in the story.

00:02:02.872 --> 00:02:03.915
Walking into Jane's den

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:06.793
it was so immediately inspiring

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:11.631
because I could just dive into a world that she had already created.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:16.719
The clothes really are a symbol of Cora and Will's story.

00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:22.058
It just felt like we could break rules and it would still feel authentic.

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:27.021
It doesn't feel like a constrained, buttoned up drama.

00:02:27.021 --> 00:02:30.233
It feels liberating, it feels incredibly fresh.

00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:37.198
It has a very kind of contemporary and visceral and immediate feeling

00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:40.410
and so it's just been really fantastic

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.704
and they're just really beautiful.

